\n   \\[\n   (b^4 + b^3 + b + 1) \\cdot (b-1) = b^5 - b^4 + b^4 - b^3 + b^2 - b + b - 1 = b^5 + b^2 - 1\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert the base-\\(b\\) number \\(1001_b\\) to base-10:**\n   \\[\n   1001_b = 1 \\cdot b^3 + 0 \\cdot b^2 + 0 \\cdot b + 1 = b^3 + 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the two base-10 numbers:**\n   \\[\n   (b^5 + b^2 - 1) + (b^3 + 1) = b^5 + b^3 + b^2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Convert the base-10 number \\(b^5 + b^3 + b^2\\) back to base-\\(b\\):**\n   The number \\(b^5 + b^3 + b^2\\) in base-10 is equivalent to \\(10101_b\\) in base-\\(b\\).\n\nTherefore, the result is \\(\\boxed{10101_b}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{10101_b}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:451"}
